WEBVTT

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.180
Good morning, Mr. Aramaki.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.060
Good morning.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.810
Did you sleep well?

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:23.270
Yes, thanks to all of you.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.770
It's been a long time since I've slept
with a roof over my head.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.360
It made me happy. Thank you.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.280
We all built it together.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.280
But lately, it leaks a lot
because of all the rain.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:36.740
It will keep raining.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.950
The rainy season has only just begun.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.870
-The rainy season?
-Hey.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.370
Is it true you really wandered around
on your own for 15 years?

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.000
It is.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.540
You sure clean up well.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.460
To us, you're a real sight for sore eyes.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.970
Can I interest you in a morning bath,
Mr. Aramaki?

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:55.380
Sure.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.640
-I really love taking baths now.
-Hey.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.600
I'm not sure if it's wise for us
to trust this guy so easily.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.850
-If you want, I'll wash your back for you.
-You think so?

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:04.560
Well, he is handsome though.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.900
Time for breakfast, everyone!

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.400
-Okay.
-Much appreciated.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.110
-Out of the way.
-Sorry about that.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:12.940
Stay away from me, you filthy dogs.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:14.490
Oh, my apologies.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:16.990
Diamond, Battery, calm down.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:19.910
Fubuki, Miss Mitsuru,
please keep an eye on them.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:21.950
Why do you only call that one "Miss"?

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:22.870
What?

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.660
Oh, because she's a lady.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.290
Her namesake was very beautiful.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:31.710
<i>He said he once traveled
with two people who had those names.</i>

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:34.720
<i>I don't know if what he says is true,</i>

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:37.930
<i>but he doesn't seem like
a bad person to me.</i>

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:08.890
GRAIN RAIN

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.650
<i>You've been to the storage shelter
in Hokkaido, right?</i>

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.560
Yes, I found that one.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.820
Was there some sort of statue
to mark its location?

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.990
Oh, yes. There was.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:22.410
A figure with many arms
was carved into the nearby rocks.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.410
The thousand-armed Avalokiteshvara.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:25.870
It figures.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.580
What does?

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.620
That's the guardian deity of the north.

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:33.040
I like that kind of stuff.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:35.290
Anyway, how about the Tohoku region?

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:38.460
I didn't find a shelter there.
The climate was warmer than in Hokkaido.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.720
Can someone really last
15 years out here all alone?

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:44.220
-There were no tiger-like beasts either.
-If he did, he might be crazy.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.470
If he's lying, he has an ulterior motive.

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:48.970
The dogs were with him.
That makes a huge difference.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.190
That hurt!

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:55.400
You need more practice.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.360
Oh, hush, Momotaro.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:58.780
That looks like fun.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:03.280
You would think so, but I can't figure out
how to control it very well.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.410
Oh, shoot! It's stuck up there.

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:10.870
Well, it's useless now.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.460
A perfect strike.

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:19.130
Oh, would you mind doing that again?

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:20.590
A straight throw.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.010
Sure.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.020
Takahiro Aramaki...

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:36.350
This guy and Fubuki Samejima from
Hiroshima are destined for the majors.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:39.900
Watching them play
really helps motivate me.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:42.780
Fubuki?

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.240
Do you mean Fubuki Samejima?

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:46.950
He was there with you?

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:51.450
And by Miss Mitsuru,
do you mean Mitsuru Kagurazaka?

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.580
Yes.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:54.580
Were you a friend of hers?

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:59.040
No, but anyone who does
traditional Japanese dancing knows her.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:00.880
So she passed away?

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.170
That's such a shame.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:04.720
We should be the same age.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:08.140
I saw you in the Koshien Tournament on TV.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:09.600
Right.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:14.600
But I've lived for 15 years
more than you all have.

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:26.200
Okay, come here.

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:32.290
Charcoal?

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:35.410
It looks like someone lit a fire here.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.580
But who?

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:39.330
Well, it might have been those three.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:44.340
Some time ago, I ran across three people
traveling near Tokyo.

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:47.550
I wonder if they're the same people
who left that note in the shelter?

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:49.760
Was one of them a girl
named Natsu Iwashimizu?

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:51.760
I never got their names.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:58.650
"This was the only voyage which I may say
was successful in all my..."

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.900
What can you tell me about those three?

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:07.570
One looked like a serious athlete type,
the other had long hair,

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:09.820
and the last was a quiet young girl.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:12.450
What about the athlete's hair
and his height?

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:15.040
He was slightly shorter than me.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.580
I actually saved him from drowning.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:19.500
-Drowning?
-Yes.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:22.630
However, they were suspicious of me
and departed rather quickly.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:25.420
I should have asked for their names
when I had the chance.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:28.220
<i>No, that can't be Arashi.</i>

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.590
<i>He was always a good swimmer.</i>

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.100
-It started raining.
-Let's go back.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:35.850
Let's get going, Ms. Hana.

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:37.060
Oh, right.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:45.610
Ouch.

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:51.110
What is this weird, gooey, purple stuff?

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:02.960
I feel like this is definitely from
the first half of <i>Robinson Crusoe</i>.

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:06.460
I have the second half
that I borrowed from Arashi.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:08.050
Is it just a coincidence?

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:10.630
But even if it isn't,

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:13.850
if I saw Arashi again,

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:16.220
would he still be the same person?

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.100
If he woke up earlier than we did, then...

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:23.560
<i>Even if he did, I still need to find him.</i>

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:26.230
<i>Arashi will always be Arashi to me.</i>

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:28.820
<i>You've sure got it good, Hana.</i>

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:29.740
<i>What do you mean?</i>

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:31.780
Having someone you love.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:35.200
That's what keeps you so optimistic.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:36.870
I'm not so sure.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.450
What about you, Fujiko?
Is there someone you're fond of?

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:46.210
I wouldn't say "fond," but there
used to be someone I looked up to.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:47.380
A doctor.

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:48.710
Oh, that's news to me.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.550
I had a sneaking suspicion.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:53.180
He did volunteer work overseas and such.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:56.140
Actually, that was where we first met.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:00.480
There was a civil war
and a lot of people got injured.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:03.310
It was a shocking experience.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:05.360
This one guy's guts were coming out.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:07.900
When I tried to push them back in,
he shouted at me,

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.440
"Don't just shove them back in!"

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:12.400
You pushed a guy's guts back in?

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:14.410
I just want to faint at the thought.

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:18.330
I looked up to him,
but I wouldn't search for him now.

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:21.910
That must mean my feelings are
different from yours, Hana.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.420
Makes sense.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.420
Well, what do you think about Tsunomata?

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:29.210
I don't really like
a guy who avoids conflict.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.550
Well then, how about Mr. Aramaki?

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:35.050
I was really suspicious of him at first,

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:37.970
but he turned out to be
quite handsome after he shaved.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.470
So it all comes down to looks with you?

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:41.680
I'm surprised.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.360
Well, it's about time for lights-out.
Okay, Hana?

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:50.980
Oh, sure.

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:56.450
<i>It has started to spread.</i>

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:02.330
Ms. Hana, you shouldn't go this far
all by yourself.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:04.580
Stand back!

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:07.790
This stuff shows up
early in the rainy season.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:11.380
It turns whatever plants and animals
it touches into slush.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:14.340
Is there a cure?

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.380
I don't know.

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:19.350
It might be a poison, or a fungus,
or something entirely unknown.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:23.140
But we'll be fine
as long as we don't touch it.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.730
If we don't touch it...

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.900
It's on the verge of death, now.
It can't move anymore.

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:32.780
Turn to slush...

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:35.150
<i>There has to be...</i>

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:37.160
<i>some kind of medicine.</i>

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:38.910
<i>For boils or rashes,</i>

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:41.660
aloe vera, chamomile,
or even plantains would help.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:44.450
Where the hell am I going to find
any of those?

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:51.250
I should talk to Fujiko.

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:54.210
She might know of some way to treat this.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:56.130
No, I can't.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.130
I don't want to worry anyone.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:00.890
And what's worse, it may spread to them
if they touch me.

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:02.260
Are you in there, Hana?

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:03.600
Are you ready to take a bath?

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:04.770
Maybe later.

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:06.770
Okay, we'll take ours first.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:12.690
If I stay here like this,

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:16.190
I'll just become a problem for everyone.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.950
That means I only have one choice.

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:34.550
Wait a minute.

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:37.090
I'm dead either way, so...

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.950
This was for the best, right?

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:04.580
Right?

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:10.960
"I'm leaving to look for my boyfriend.
Fujiko, I'm sorry for not telling you."

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.290
Why would she do this?

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:16.550
Now that you mention it, I noticed
she seemed down these past few days.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:22.220
But even so, you would think she would
at least come and talk to me.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:28.020
I thought we were close enough
to be honest with each other.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:30.180
I bet she just didn't want us to worry.

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:32.690
It still pisses me off.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.270
Hana, why did you keep to yourself?

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.320
The current is getting stronger.

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:41.490
I'm starving.

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:44.530
Why am I even complaining?

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.450
I should just let it go. There's no point.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.330
You made up your mind and gave up, right?

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:00.090
<i>It hurts! My whole body hurts!</i>

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:02.510
<i>I can't take this anymore.</i>

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:06.550
<i>I just... want it all to end.</i>

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:08.930
Ms. Hana!

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.480
Over here! Come on!

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:17.900
What are you doing? Hurry up!

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:20.690
It's too late, just...

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:22.530
leave me here.

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:24.110
Don't give up!

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:35.460
The game doesn't end
until the umpire calls the final out.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:39.210
I finally met you after all this time.

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:42.340
I will not let you die!

00:12:55.520 --> 00:13:00.480
We could see you, but the strong current
made it hard to catch up.

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:02.650
I'm glad we never lost sight of you.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:05.200
Don't! Stay away from me!

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:08.240
Is it that purple stuff?

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:10.830
There's no cure, right?

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.870
You should just leave me behind.

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:15.830
That's true. I don't know how to cure it.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:20.210
But I feel that, if we take a closer look,
there must be a hint.

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:22.710
We just need to figure out what it is.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:24.050
Stay back!

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:26.010
It will spread if you touch it.

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:34.520
I see an island.

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:37.850
It kind of looks like a cat.

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:41.900
The ocean looks rough.

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:43.900
Let's stay here for a while.

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:44.860
Right.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:48.160
I'm sorry I caused all this trouble.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:52.540
It would have been better
if you two had stayed with everyone else.

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:54.120
You don't need to apologize.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:56.580
I came here of my own free will.

00:13:57.460 --> 00:14:00.380
So I don't have any regrets about it.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:04.380
Why are you being so kind to me?

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:09.550
We only just met
and you hardly know anything about me.

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:12.930
It may be difficult for you to understand

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:15.680
just how much
I wanted to meet another person.

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:20.650
When you smiled at me,
it was a moment of pure joy.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:25.150
Hana.

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:26.990
I'm taking requests.

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:29.700
Then play a funeral march.

00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:30.950
No jokes.

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:33.700
Okay, play "Morning Mood" again.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:53.430
Her fever must be getting worse.

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:55.560
She's struggling to breathe.

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:01.480
-Maybe what we need is salt.
-Salt?

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:04.320
Do you remember when Battery
jumped close to Ms. Hana?

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:06.650
Yes, Mitsuru dunked him
in the ocean water.

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:07.610
Exactly.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:09.990
I wonder if it's vulnerable to salt.

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:13.910
There was none of that purple stuff
near the coast at all.

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:18.000
If only we had a water source
with a higher concentration of salt.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:20.080
I'll go look for some.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:21.330
Please do.

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:31.590
Are you awake?

00:15:31.970 --> 00:15:33.300
What's that?

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:34.890
I boiled down some ocean water.

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:38.470
This is going to sting, but hang in there.

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:41.230
It hurts!

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:43.100
I'm going to fetch more water.

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:45.310
I'll be back soon.

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:47.940
Fubuki, keep an eye on her.

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:49.820
Miss Mitsuru, with me.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:56.490
<i>Dad always used to tell me,</i>

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:59.370
<i>"Unless you can decide
and act on your own,</i>

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:02.540
<i>then you won't survive during a crisis."</i>

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:04.500
<i>Also,</i>

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.710
<i>"Make sure to end things
on your own terms."</i>

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:11.090
Wait, was Dad really the one
who told me that?

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:16.180
Thank you, Mr. Aramaki and Haru.

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:17.510
I'm so sorry.

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:26.520
This island is where things come to die.

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:33.110
It feels so nice and cool.

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:37.490
<i>Do you want to die, Hana?</i>

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:39.490
All you have to do is say it.

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:41.040
"I want to die."

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:44.580
Before you fester and rot,
say "I want to die."

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:47.000
That's the reason I'm here.

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:49.250
I'm here for you.

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:55.220
Am I dreaming? Who is this man?

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:57.470
Do you want to die, Hana?

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:00.680
Oh, you're the Grim Reaper.

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:02.770
That's right.

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:06.440
I left everyone behind
with the intention of dying.

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:15.200
Is that a wall painting?

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:16.700
TEAM SUMMER B WAS HERE.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:19.700
ARASHI AOTA

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:20.870
Arashi...

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:22.700
has been here.

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:24.790
Arashi is...

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:26.670
still alive.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:28.540
I'll kill you now

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:30.550
before you have to suffer.

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:32.590
I don't...

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:34.510
want to die.

00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:36.510
I don't want to die.

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:38.180
Let go of me!

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:40.390
I won't die here!

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:41.680
I refuse to die!

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:43.720
Get lost, Grim Reaper!

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:53.440
ARASHI AOTA - FOR HANA: LET'S MEET AGAIN

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:55.440
Arashi...

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:00.450
Ms. Hana!

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:03.950
Ms. Hana, what is this?

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:05.040
He's here...

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:07.290
Arashi is still alive.

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:10.960
Arashi Aota, the man I love.

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:16.630
He must have the power to draw you to him.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:19.470
Haru found it.

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:21.350
A way to save you.

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:23.680
Let's go, Ms. Hana. Can you walk?

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:27.560
Yes, I can walk. I will walk.

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:28.980
I want to walk.

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:33.980
Thanks so much, both of you.

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:35.400
I'm going.

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:37.320
Ms. Hana!

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:47.120
What are the odds that two people in love
would both get picked for this project?

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:48.710
It could have been deliberate.

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:50.540
Deliberate when it comes to love?

00:18:53.420 --> 00:18:56.960
Well, perhaps they were betting
that love might make a difference.

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:01.640
<i>What? You want to look for him?</i>

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:02.640
Yes.

00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:06.850
I know that we don't even know
where we are, but I want to look for him.

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:09.640
I realize it's selfish, but please.

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:12.520
-I figured you might say that.
-What?

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:14.520
Once you feel better, we'll go together.

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:17.690
What? Do you really think
we would just let you go alone?

00:19:18.110 --> 00:19:20.450
If we did that, you would just
get yourself in trouble again.

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:23.910
Thanks, Haru. You too, Mr. Aramaki.

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:26.910
But if the boy I met
was really Arashi, then...

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:29.660
<i>I'm a little concerned,
because he seemed like</i>

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:31.830
he had already lost hope.

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:40.340
I thought you liked having long hair.

00:19:40.420 --> 00:19:41.380
I do,

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:44.850
but I hate the split-ends
that make my hair look like a bird's nest.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:49.140
Wow, that pocket knife is really useful.

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:50.350
Yes.

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:53.730
It's something
that my father really treasured.

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:57.610
Do you want me to get rid of
those annoying bangs for you?

00:19:57.690 --> 00:19:59.280
These are part of my style.

00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:01.450
How about you get a cut, Mr. Aramaki?

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:04.280
The fish are dead.

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:07.580
Is that ash?

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:09.330
A volcano must have erupted.

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:17.380
<i>Dear Arashi, Semimaru, Nat, and Mozu.</i>

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:20.380
"Arashi"? This must be from Team Summer B.

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:23.180
<i>Ashes have been falling
for a few days now.</i>

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:25.640
<i>They piled up more than
a meter deep very quickly.</i>

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:29.010
<i>We definitely can't survive here,
so we're moving.</i>

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:31.770
<i>We will make our way towards
Mt. Kobe Fuji.</i>

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:35.350
So, it's from the other members
of Arashi's team.

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:37.230
I can't read this name, what is it?

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:38.440
It's pronounced "Mozu."

00:20:38.980 --> 00:20:41.280
Prime Minister Mozunoto spells
his name the same way, right?

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:44.950
<i>"Mozu"? Was he that man?</i>

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:46.820
Ms. Hana.

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:50.240
We should also head east.

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:58.460
Goddamn it! I don't know how many more
days of this rain I can take!

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:01.710
Meanwhile, this gloomy lug is
about to start growing mold.

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:05.720
So what books did you like
when you were a kid?

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:09.430
What? Oh, I liked <i>No No Nursery School</i>
I guess.

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:11.060
I've never heard of it.

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:12.390
I loved that book, too.

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:15.230
They built a boat from blocks
and pretended to hunt for whales, right?

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:17.940
The S.S. Elephant n' Lion.

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:22.900
What?

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:24.110
Going to the bathroom, I bet.

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:25.280
I see...

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:40.500
Semimaru!

00:21:40.590 --> 00:21:42.210
How long are you going to mope?

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:47.510
If moping really makes a difference,
then keep moping.

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:49.010
-But--
-I know.

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:52.560
I know,
but hearing you say it ticks me off.

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:56.350
Hey! What's wrong?

00:21:56.890 --> 00:21:58.900
I let the pot float away.

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:00.440
Jeez, you're such a klutz.

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:03.440
That pot is the only big one that we have.

00:22:03.530 --> 00:22:04.690
Not my problem.

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:05.900
I'll take care of it.

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:10.570
<i>Arashi...</i>

00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:18.670
Sorry about everything!

00:22:18.750 --> 00:22:21.920
I really appreciate what you've done,
Ms. Iwashimizu, Semimaru!

00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:27.510
It's nothing. And please, call me Natsu.

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:29.720
Natsu!

00:22:29.930 --> 00:22:32.510
Just look at her hitting on him.

00:22:35.520 --> 00:22:36.980
<i>Isn't that...</i>

00:22:37.060 --> 00:22:40.440
Way to go, Arashi! This is definitely
another one of those shelters.

00:22:40.520 --> 00:22:42.310
We can finally eat some rice again.

00:22:42.400 --> 00:22:43.730
What's over there?

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:49.070
Amazing.

00:22:49.150 --> 00:22:52.240
They left this here for us to use, right?

00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:54.740
I know just what to name it.

00:22:55.370 --> 00:22:56.580
The S.S. Elephant n' Lion.

00:22:59.920 --> 00:23:02.460
Looks like Team Autumn's village was
buried by the ash, too.

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:04.590
Even after building this whole village,

00:23:05.300 --> 00:23:07.590
they were still forced to move on.

00:23:08.170 --> 00:23:10.630
You realize nobody is
going to return to this place.

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:11.680
I know.

00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:14.760
But even so,
I want to leave something behind.

00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:24.650
Do you mind if I make a quick stop?

00:23:24.730 --> 00:23:25.690
Go ahead.

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:33.120
This hat belonged to Fubuki.

00:23:34.030 --> 00:23:36.740
I'm sure Fubuki's spirit is here with us.

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:40.330
<i>Summer days come once again</i>

00:23:41.040 --> 00:23:43.880
<i>Time, please stop just this once</i>

00:23:45.340 --> 00:23:47.090
<i>For the youth who brought a miracle</i>

00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:49.670
<i>Clouds dance with excitement</i>

00:23:49.760 --> 00:23:51.010
<i>At Koshien</i>

00:23:51.840 --> 00:23:52.760
<i>Bring it on.</i>

00:23:55.260 --> 00:23:56.760
<i>Fubuki!</i>
